.TH DOTF 1 "2026-03-14" "dotf 3.0.12" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dotf \- modular dotfile manager using git bare repo with sparse checkout
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dotf
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dotf
manages dotfiles through a git bare repository at \fI~/.dotf/\fR with sparse
checkout.
Files are organized into plugins (logical groups) and profiles (sets of
plugins).
Running
.B dotf
with no arguments launches the interactive TUI.
.SH SETUP COMMANDS
.TP
.B init \fIREPO_URL\fR [\-p \fINAME\fR]
Clone a bare repo from \fIREPO_URL\fR and set up sparse checkout.
Optionally activate profile \fINAME\fR after clone.
.TP
.B new
Create a new bare repository at \fI~/.dotf/\fR.
.TP
.B migrate
Scaffold v3 metadata files on an existing bare repo.
.SH PLUGIN COMMANDS
.TP
.B plugin list
List all defined plugins.
.TP
.B plugin new \fINAME\fR [\-\-desc \fITEXT\fR]
Create a new plugin with optional description.
.TP
.B plugin delete \fINAME\fR
Delete a plugin definition.
.TP
.B plugin install \fINAME\fR...
Install one or more plugins (resolves dependencies via topological sort).
.TP
.B plugin remove \fINAME\fR...
Remove one or more installed plugins.
.TP
.B plugin info \fINAME\fR
Show detailed information about a plugin.
.SH PROFILE COMMANDS
.TP
.B profile list
List all defined profiles.
.TP
.B profile new \fINAME\fR \-\-plugins \fIa,b,c\fR
Create a profile with the given comma-separated plugin list.
.TP
.B profile delete \fINAME\fR
Delete a profile definition.
.TP
.B profile activate \fINAME\fR
Activate a profile, installing its plugins.
.TP
.B profile deactivate
Deactivate the current profile.
.TP
.B profile show
Show the currently active profile.
.SH TRACKING COMMANDS
.TP
.B track \fIFILE\fR [\-p \fINAME\fR]
Start tracking a file. Optionally assign it to plugin \fINAME\fR.
.TP
.B untrack \fIFILE\fR
Stop tracking a file.
.TP
.B ignore \fIPATTERN\fR
Add a pattern to \fI.gitignore\fR.
.TP
.B freeze \fIFILE\fR
Freeze a tracked file (set skip-worktree bit). Local changes will not appear
in status or be committed.
.TP
.B unfreeze \fIFILE\fR
Unfreeze a previously frozen file.
.TP
.B frozen
List all frozen files.
.SH DISCOVERY COMMANDS
.TP
.B untracked [\-p \fINAME\fR]
List untracked files. Optionally scope to a plugin's watch paths.
.TP
.B watchlist add \fIPATH\fR
Add a path to the watchlist.
.TP
.B watchlist remove \fIPATH\fR
Remove a path from the watchlist.
.TP
.B watchlist list
List all watchlist paths.
.SH SAVE & GIT COMMANDS
.TP
.B save [\fIMSG\fR]
Auto-stage tracked changes, commit with optional message, and push.
.TP
.B stage \fIFILE\fR...
Stage one or more files.
.TP
.B unstage \fIFILE\fR...
Unstage one or more files.
.TP
.B commit [\fIMSG\fR]
Commit staged changes with optional message.
.TP
.B push
Push to the remote repository.
.TP
.B pull
Pull from the remote repository.
.TP
.B status
Show git status of tracked dotfiles.
.TP
.B diff
Show git diff of tracked dotfiles.
.TP
.B git \fIARGS\fR...
Pass arguments directly to git (bare repo context).
.SH MAINTENANCE COMMANDS
.TP
.B consolidate [\-\-apply]
Consolidate plugin paths. Runs as dry-run by default; pass \fB\-\-apply\fR to
execute changes.
.TP
.B packages [\-\-install]
List OS packages for active plugins. Pass \fB\-\-install\fR to install missing
packages.
.SH AI-ASSISTED COMMANDS
.TP
.B suggest\-ignore
AI-assisted gitignore pattern suggestions.
.TP
.B suggest\-assign
AI-assisted file-to-plugin assignment.
.TP
.B resolve
AI-assisted merge conflict resolution.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Getting started
Clone an existing dotfile repo and activate a profile:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ dotf init git@github.com:user/dotfiles.git \-p workstation
.fi
.RE
.PP
Or start from scratch:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ dotf new
.fi
.RE
.SS Plugin workflow
Create a plugin, track files into it, then install:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ dotf plugin new zsh \-\-desc "Zsh configuration"
$ dotf track ~/.zshrc \-p zsh
$ dotf track ~/.zshenv \-p zsh
$ dotf plugin install zsh
.fi
.RE
.PP
Install multiple plugins at once (dependencies resolved automatically):
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ dotf plugin install neovim tmux git
.fi
.RE
.PP
Inspect a plugin's files and dependencies:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ dotf plugin info neovim
.fi
.RE
.SS Profile workflow
Create a profile grouping several plugins, then activate it:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ dotf profile new laptop \-\-plugins zsh,neovim,tmux,git
$ dotf profile activate laptop
.fi
.RE
.PP
Switch machines by activating a different profile:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ dotf profile activate server
.fi
.RE
.SS Day-to-day usage
Quick save \(em stages all tracked changes, commits, and pushes:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ dotf save "update neovim config"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Or do it step by step:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ dotf status
$ dotf stage ~/.config/nvim/init.lua
$ dotf commit "tweak nvim keybindings"
$ dotf push
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check what's not yet tracked:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ dotf untracked
$ dotf untracked \-p zsh
.fi
.RE
.SS Freezing files
Freeze a file to keep local changes out of commits:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ dotf freeze ~/.config/settings.json
$ dotf frozen
$ dotf unfreeze ~/.config/settings.json
.fi
.RE
.SS Watchlist
Monitor directories for new untracked files:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ dotf watchlist add ~/.config/nvim
$ dotf watchlist list
.fi
.RE
.SS Maintenance
Dry-run path consolidation, then apply:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ dotf consolidate
$ dotf consolidate \-\-apply
.fi
.RE
.PP
List or install OS packages declared by active plugins:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ dotf packages
$ dotf packages \-\-install
.fi
.RE
.SS Raw git access
Pass arbitrary git commands through the bare repo:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ dotf git log \-\-oneline \-10
$ dotf git remote \-v
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version information.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show help text.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.dotf/
Git bare repository.
.TP
.I ~/.config/dotf/plugins.yaml
Plugin definitions and watchlist (tracked).
.TP
.I ~/.config/dotf/profiles.yaml
Profile definitions (tracked).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/dotf/state.yaml
Runtime state: active profile, installed plugins (not tracked).
